-- title:
--   A single archimedean window for weighted split orbital integrals
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $\nu_{Z_K}$ a Haar measure on $(\mathbb A_K)^\times$, and $u\in K^\times$ with $u\neq 1$ in $K$. Let $fa:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)\to\mathbb C$ satisfy `IsArchTestFactor`, i.e. $fa$ has compact support and $fa(g)=\Phi$ of the matrix of archimedean entries of $g$ (transported to the mixed space) for some $C^\infty$ function $\Phi$; let $c_{\tau K}>0$, and let $\nu_A$ be a Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_\infty)$ for the Borel structure. Put $\gamma(z)=\mathrm{scalar}(z)\cdot\mathrm{diag}(\iota u,1)$ for $z\in(\mathbb A_K)^\times$. The data $(\tau_G,\tau_A,\tau_F,c_T)$ are Haar measures on the centralizer of $\gamma(z)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_K)$, on the centralizer of its archimedean component, and on the local centralizers of its $v$-components, subject to: each $\tau_F(z,v)$ gives mass $1$ to the set of elements with $g$ and $g^{-1}$ integral at $v$; $\int_{\,\cdot}g\,d\tau_G(z)=c_{\tau K}\int g(\mathrm{diag}(p_1,p_2))\,d(\nu_{Z_K}\times\nu_{Z_K})$ for all $g$; and a restricted-product formula $\int W\,d\tau_G(z)=c_T\big(\int W_\infty\,d\tau_A(z)\big)\prod_{v\in S'}\int W_v\,d\tau_F(z,v)$ for measurable factorizable $W$ vanishing off the integral locus outside $S'$. Then there is a continuous compactly supported $\Psi$ on $(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\to$ mixed space of $K$, nonvanishing only at pairs of units, with $\mathrm{tsupport}\,\Psi$ contained in the image of a compact set of pairs in $(K_\infty)^\times$, such that for every $z$ and every $J$ that is a weighted orbital integral value of $fa$ at the archimedean component of $\gamma(z)$ relative to $(\nu_A,\tau_A(z))$ with weight $y\mapsto-\log H(y)-\log H(w_\infty y)$ ($H$ the product of local heights $|\det|/\mathrm{rowNormSq}$, $w_\infty$ the archimedean component of the adelic Weyl element), one has $J=\Psi(\iota(u_\infty),\iota(z_\infty))$.
--
--   This packages the archimedean weighted orbital integrals of Arthur's trace formula along the family of split regular classes $\mathrm{scalar}(z)\mathrm{diag}(u,1)$ into one continuous compactly supported window function of the pair $(u_\infty,z_\infty)$, with the weight given by the log-height of $y$ and of its Weyl translate. It is used in the assembly of weighted class integrals and in the integrability and local-constancy statements for the windowed trace-formula comparison.
